# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Wrangler local state/temp (Cloudflare Workers deploy) — never committed.
.wrangler/

# Reference data — researchers' data must never be committed (FOUNDATIONS §6).
# Ignore ALL of data/ (not just *.mat): CSV/JSON derived from recordings are
# raw-adjacent and must not leak either. Only a README may be tracked, so the
# directory's purpose is documented without shipping any data.
# Promote a file to a golden test asset deliberately, never by accident.
data/*
!data/README.md

# darkroom/ — local-only figures developed from reference data (never committed).
darkroom/

# exports/ — CSV produced by scripts/mat2csv.py from reference .mat data.
# Researchers' data must never be committed (FOUNDATIONS §6); the converter is
# tracked, its output is not.
exports/

# R session byproducts
.Rhistory
.RData

# Python bytecode (from scripts/, e.g. mat2csv.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local scratch working prompts (never committed)
TAB1_NOISE_PROMPT.md

# Relics of copying MATLAB source into this tree while porting it to Vite/Svelte.
# The canonical copies live in the `interface2` repo (APViewer is its own project
# on branch ap-summary-pdf); the copies here were byte-identical leftovers and are
# deleted. These guard rules keep the port from silently re-dropping them into the
# SCM view. (The DELIBERATE MATLAB reference — TDdeconvStack.m, aCa98_batch_APs.m,
# spikeTriggeredAverage.m — stays tracked as the Tab 2 source-of-truth.)
MATLAB CODE/APViewer/
MATLAB CODE/minBarF2.m

# Local Claude Code settings — machine-specific (absolute worktree paths, a
# personal permission allow-list). Not shared-team content.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local working notes — scratch area, kept out of the repo.
docs/notes/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
